window.docContents[204].resolve({"/Measures-and-the-Iwasawa-algebra/#An-introduction-to-p-adic-L-functions-___-Lean-blueprint--Measures-and-the-Iwasawa-algebra":{"contents":"This chapter develops the -adic analysis underlying the whole story: -adic\nmeasures on a profinite abelian group , their identification with the Iwasawa\nalgebra , and — in the key case  — a fourth description as\npower series via the Mahler transform. We then build a toolbox of operations on\nmeasures, introduce pseudo-measures (to accommodate the simple pole of the zeta\nfunction), and close with locally analytic distributions. The treatment follows\n §3.\n\nThroughout we fix a finite extension  of , with -adic valuation\n normalised by ; this is the coefficient field, and \ndenotes its ring of integers.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"An introduction to p-adic L-functions — Lean blueprint","header":"3. Measures and the Iwasawa algebra","id":"/Measures-and-the-Iwasawa-algebra/#An-introduction-to-p-adic-L-functions-___-Lean-blueprint--Measures-and-the-Iwasawa-algebra"}});